            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say home, then write the roof from 字 and the whole character 字."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "Script — the shape",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "宀 + 豕 becomes 家 (jiā)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Finish the three-stroke roof first. Under it, write the lower body from its top horizontal through the centre curve, three left-falling strokes, and the long right-falling finish. Ten strokes; nine lifts."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The old lower component is 豕, livestock. That decomposition is real history and a useful shape boundary. It is not a claim that a present-day home or family is defined by an animal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Trace 家 (jiā) once. Copy it once, saying roof, then body."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
